PROJECT STRUCTURE
-----------------

com.androidtutorials
│
├── androidhelloworld      // Main application entry package. Usually contains MainActivity, Application class, and app startup logic. This is where the app starts executing.
│
├── data                   // Responsible for handling WHERE the data comes from (API, Database, Cache, Files). Implements repository logic and manages data sources.
│   ├── local              // Handles local storage such as Room Database. Contains DAO interfaces, database classes, and Entity models used for storing data locally.
│   ├── mapper             // Converts models between layers. Example: API model (UserDto) → Database model (UserEntity) → Domain model (User). Keeps layers independent.
│   ├── model              // Contains API response models that match server JSON structure. Example: UserDto, LoginResponse, ProductDto.
│   ├── remote             // Handles network communication. Contains Retrofit API interfaces that define server endpoints and HTTP requests.
│   └── repository         // Implements repository interfaces defined in the domain layer. Combines API calls and database operations to provide data to the domain layer.
│
├── domain                 // Core business logic layer. Independent of Android framework. Contains pure Kotlin code with no dependency on Retrofit, Room, or Android classes.
│   ├── model              // Business models used throughout the app. Clean data models not tied to API or database structures. Example: User, Product, Order.
│   ├── repository         // Repository interfaces that define what operations the app can perform (e.g., fetch users, login user). Implementation exists in data layer.
│   └── usecase            // Represents a single business operation or action. Example: GetUsersUseCase, LoginUseCase, UploadFileUseCase. Called by ViewModel.
│
└── presentation           // UI layer responsible for displaying data and handling user interaction. Communicates with the domain layer through ViewModels.
├── adapter            // RecyclerView adapters used to bind data to list UI components. Example: UserAdapter, ProductAdapter.
├── ui                 // UI screens such as Activities, Fragments, or Compose screens. Responsible only for displaying UI and observing ViewModel state.
└── viewmodel          // Bridge between UI and domain layer. Calls use cases, prepares UI state, and survives configuration changes like screen rotation.


APPLICATION FLOW
----------------

MainActivity (UI Layer)
↓
UserViewModel (Presentation Layer)
↓
GetUsersUseCase (Domain Layer)
↓
UserRepository Interface (Domain Layer)
↓
UserRepositoryImpl (Data Layer)
↓
ApiService or UserDao (Network / Database)
↓
Data returned to ViewModel
↓
UI updated


SIMPLE MEMORY RULE
------------------

presentation → HOW data is shown to the user
domain       → WHAT business operation the app performs
data         → WHERE the data comes from